      "problem": "Simplify the expression $\\left|-\\dfrac{9}{5c}\\right|.$",
      "worked_solution": "Firstly, since $|-a| = |a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n\\left|\\dfrac{9}{5c}\\right|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the division, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{9}{5c}| & = \\\\ \\frac{|9|}{|5c|} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{|5c|} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{|5|\\cdot |c|} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{5|c|}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
